--   KappaBound (2⁻¹⁸²) from the machine alone
-- statement:
--   **`KappaBound (2⁻¹⁸²)` from the machine alone.** With the explicit parameters of §9.2 and `n₀ = 2^{2^{2^{132}}}`, the only remaining hypotheses concern the multitape machine: it is correct for every `n ≥ 1`, and for `n ≥ n₀` it runs in time `C₀ (V(n) · Ncost(p, d, K, ℓ, α) + n)` (Table 1 normalized cost).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.GlueParams`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.OpenAI.Glue.kappaBound_of_machine (M : IntMul.MultitapeTM)
--       (hcorr : ∀ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n → ∃ T : ℝ, IntMul.MultipliesAt M n T)
--       (C₀ : ℝ) (hC₀ : 0 ≤ C₀)
--       (htime : ∀ n, n0 ≤ n → IntMul.MultipliesAt M n
--         (C₀ * (VP n * Ncost (6 * (IntMul.lg n : ℝ)) (dP n) (KP n) (ℓP n) (αP n) + n))) :
--       IntMul.KappaBound (1 / 2 ^ 182)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *Glue 3: explicit parameters `n ↦ (b, L, T, d, K, ℓ, α, p)` of §9.2 and the threshold `n₀`*: For an input length `n` (§9.2.1):
--   * `b = lg n` (`bP`), `p = 6b` (`pP`), `d = ⌊b^ε⌋` (`dP`), `K = ⌊d^c⌋` (`KP`),
--     `α = ⌈(12 d² b)^{1/4}⌉` (`αP`);
--   * `L` (`LP`) = the least `L` with `4n ≤ 2^L b`, `T = 2^L` (`TP`), so `4n ≤ T b < 8n`;
--   * `ℓ = ⌈L/d⌉` (`ℓP`, `RP.ell`), `r = 2^ℓ` (`rP`), bit volume `V = T p` (`VP`), `γ = 2dα²` (`γP`).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** This lemma belongs to the Lean formalization (integer-multiplication-kappa campaign) of the OpenAI preprint *Integer multiplication below $n\log n$*: the array model of tape data (mixed-radix arrays and pull maps), the interchange networks of §3–4 (Propositions 7, 8, 11, Lemmas 9–12), the butterfly layers of §5 (Lemma 13, Proposition 14), the synthesis of §6–7 (Lemma 16, Proposition 18), the resampling and parameter choices of §8–9, and the final glue `IntMul.OpenAI.Glue.kappaBound_of_machine`, which derives the platform bound `KappaBound (1/2^182)` (from `Def_IntMul_MultitapeModel`) for any correct multitape machine meeting the paper's time recurrence. All names refer to the definition bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs1`–`IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs9`.
